Today in India, for residential applications, you can use grid as battery, meaning that you can send to grid and consume whatever you want from the grid. If you consume lesser than you produced, you will get money back. If you consume more, you have to pay the delta. There is no dynamic pricing of electricity for residential users. So an integrated unit for homes is not a good enough business case. However if you consider power cuts and can add that into the equation, then it may start becoming a business case. Need to check the use case for industries.

